# [INTRO]
[00:01.20]Ta-ra-ra, ta-ra-ra
[00:05.11]Ta-ra-ra-raaa
[00:08.37]What if we choose each other?
[00:13.91]Ta-ra-ra, ta-ra-ra
# [VERSE 1]
[00:18.15]Tell me
[00:20.76]if you believe in messages from dreams
[00:25.65]If you believe in coincidence
[00:29.89]or that everything has its time
[00:34.13]What do you know
[00:37.06]of the language of the stars?
[00:40.97]The one they use in silence
[00:44.56]with which they've told a thousand stories
[00:49.13]through the ages
[00:52.06]Does chance decide our destiny
[00:56.30]or do we choose it?
[00:59.56]Did someone already choose the road
[01:03.80]or do we build it?
# [PRE-CHORUS]
[01:07.06]Maybe the answers
[01:09.99]aren't meant to be found
[01:13.90]Maybe it's choosing
[01:16.84]who to invent them with
[01:20.42]Why be spectators
[01:23.36]if we can be actors?
[01:26.29]Choose to watch life passing by
[01:30.20]or take your hand
[01:33.14]and change the perspective
# [CHORUS]
[01:37.05]WHAT IF WE CHOOSE EACH OTHER?
[01:42.27]We choose each other
[01:45.53]We invent a brand-new destiny
[01:49.77]WHOLE NEW WORLDS
[01:54.66]We are the architects
[01:58.24]of a brand-new road
[02:01.83]WHAT IF WE CHOOSE EACH OTHER?
[02:07.05]We choose each other
